{
  "title": "CHONK",
  "children": [
    {
      "title": "Overview",
      "lines": [
        "Electric bass, played",
        "not sampled.",
        "",
        "One modelled string:",
        "bridge and nut, a",
        "pickup part-way down",
        "it, a finger pluck",
        "and a strike noise.",
        "",
        "A hard note rings",
        "differently because",
        "the string is hit",
        "harder, not because a",
        "louder sample was",
        "chosen.",
        "",
        "Ported from OneTrick",
        "CHONK by Punk Labs.",
        "GPL-3.0-or-later."
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "Playing",
      "lines": [
        "Range C3-G6. Notes",
        "outside it are",
        "ignored: below, the",
        "string runs out of",
        "delay line; above, it",
        "goes unstable.",
        "",
        "Mono, by design. A",
        "new note takes the",
        "string over; letting",
        "it go hands the",
        "string back to the",
        "note below without",
        "re-plucking.",
        "",
        "Hit hard (vel 108+)",
        "and it slaps on its",
        "own."
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "Pads",
      "children": [
        {
          "title": "Articulation pads",
          "lines": [
            "The octave under the",
            "playing range:",
            "",
            "C2   Mute",
            "C#2  Slide down",
            "D2   Finger",
            "D#2  Slide up",
            "E2   Pick",
            "F2   Slap",
            "F#2  Legato",
            "G2   Ring",
            "G#2  Alt Pick",
            "",
            "They move with the",
            "octave shift, so the",
            "row stays reachable."
          ]
        },
        {
          "title": "Pad beats knob",
          "lines": [
            "A held pad always",
            "wins, and never moves",
            "the parameter.",
            "",
            "Style pads pick that",
            "style while held,",
            "then hand back to the",
            "Style setting.",
            "",
            "Mute and Legato pads",
            "INVERT their switch:",
            "with Mute latched on,",
            "hold the pad to play",
            "one open note.",
            "",
            "Slide pads bend while",
            "held, by velocity.",
            "Ring pad rings the",
            "string out."
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "Knobs",
      "lines": [
        "1 Pickup Pos",
        "2 Brightness",
        "3 Tone",
        "4 Thump",
        "5 Sustain",
        "6 Ring",
        "7 Saturation",
        "8 Volume",
        "",
        "1-3 shape the tone,",
        "4 the attack, 5-6 how",
        "long it holds and how",
        "it lets go, 7-8 the",
        "output.",
        "",
        "Pages: Attack,",
        "Fretting, Output,",
        "MIDI."
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "The string",
      "children": [
        {
          "title": "The six knobs",
          "lines": [
            "Pickup Pos moves the",
            "pickup along the",
            "string: low is fat",
            "and neck-ish, high is",
            "nasal and bridge-ish.",
            "",
            "Brightness sets how",
            "much high end the",
            "string keeps as it",
            "rings.",
            "",
            "Thump is the body of",
            "the attack, tapped",
            "straight off the",
            "finger.",
            "",
            "Tone is the passive",
            "tone control: a",
            "1-pole lowpass, 300",
            "to 2500 Hz.",
            "",
            "Sustain sets how long",
            "a held note rings."
          ]
        },
        {
          "title": "Strike Hard",
          "lines": [
            "The pick click: how",
            "hard and how bright",
            "the strike noise is.",
            "",
            "It is SUBTLE, and it",
            "is switched out of",
            "circuit whenever a",
            "Style is engaged, or",
            "above velocity 108",
            "where auto-slap takes",
            "over. Both are the",
            "original's design.",
            "",
            "If it seems dead,",
            "check Style is Off",
            "and play softer."
          ]
        },
        {
          "title": "Ring",
          "lines": [
            "How much the release",
            "damps the string.",
            "",
            "0   stopped on",
            "     release, as the",
            "     original does",
            "100 not damped at",
            "     all; it decays",
            "     on its own",
            "",
            "The G2 pad rings the",
            "string out while held",
            "whatever this says.",
            "",
            "Added by this port;",
            "0 is the original."
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "Attack",
      "children": [
        {
          "title": "Style and Strike",
          "lines": [
            "These two are the",
            "same control.",
            "",
            "A style does nothing",
            "but replace Strike",
            "Hardness with a set",
            "value:",
            "",
            "Finger 0",
            "Pick   50",
            "Slap   100",
            "Off    the knob",
            "",
            "So Strike only does",
            "anything with Style",
            "Off - and above",
            "velocity 108, where",
            "auto-slap takes over",
            "anyway.",
            "",
            "That is the original's",
            "design; they sit on",
            "one page here so it",
            "is at least visible."
          ]
        },
        {
          "title": "Mute",
          "lines": [
            "Palm mute: the string",
            "damps fast and dull,",
            "and the attack gets",
            "its own extra thump.",
            "",
            "While Mute is on, the",
            "Thump knob is out of",
            "circuit."
          ]
        },
        {
          "title": "Alt Pick",
          "lines": [
            "Alternate picking:",
            "down, up, down, up",
            "as you play, instead",
            "of every note being",
            "a downstroke.",
            "",
            "Down and up differ",
            "three ways. The pick",
            "pushes the string the",
            "other way (which is",
            "what you hear against",
            "a ringing string),",
            "the upstroke carries",
            "a little less energy,",
            "and its click is",
            "thinner and shorter.",
            "",
            "A phrase starts on a",
            "downstroke. The count",
            "restarts after a",
            "PAUSE of about 0.4 s,",
            "not when you let a",
            "note go - picking is",
            "separate notes, so",
            "releasing must not",
            "reset it.",
            "",
            "Pad G#2. Not in the",
            "original - the sizes",
            "are a guess and can",
            "be retuned.",
            "",
            "Pick Depth sets how",
            "far apart the strokes",
            "are: 100% is the",
            "voicing tuned by ear,",
            "0% leaves only the",
            "direction, 200% is",
            "twice the spread."
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "Fretting",
      "children": [
        {
          "title": "Legato",
          "lines": [
            "A sound, not a note",
            "mode.",
            "",
            "It glides the pitch",
            "over 35 ms, stepping",
            "through frets, and",
            "takes the click and",
            "the finger out of the",
            "output.",
            "",
            "Handing the string",
            "from note to note",
            "happens with Legato",
            "OFF as well - that is",
            "just how one string",
            "works."
          ]
        },
        {
          "title": "Glide and Frets",
          "lines": [
            "Legato glides the",
            "pitch; these two let",
            "you have the glide",
            "without the rest of",
            "it.",
            "",
            "Glide slides between",
            "notes over 35 ms and",
            "KEEPS the click.",
            "Legato still glides",
            "on its own, so both",
            "on is just Legato.",
            "",
            "Glide Time sets how",
            "long it takes: 0 to",
            "500 ms, higher is",
            "slower. 35 ms is the",
            "original's fixed",
            "value.",
            "",
            "Frets sets the path:",
            "on, the glide walks",
            "up the frets; off, it",
            "slides smoothly past",
            "them. On by default,",
            "which is how the",
            "original always",
            "played.",
            "",
            "Both only matter when",
            "one note is held into",
            "the next."
          ]
        },
        {
          "title": "Retrigger",
          "lines": [
            "What an overlapping",
            "note does.",
            "",
            "Off: a second note at",
            "the SAME velocity",
            "does not re-pluck -",
            "it changes the pitch",
            "of the string that is",
            "already ringing. At a",
            "different velocity it",
            "does pluck.",
            "",
            "On: every note-on",
            "plucks.",
            "",
            "Off is the original,",
            "and usually the",
            "better feel."
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "Output",
      "lines": [
        "Volume, Pan and",
        "Saturation, then five",
        "EQ bands: 100 Hz",
        "shelf, 250, 500 and",
        "1.5k peaks, 3 kHz",
        "shelf. +/-12 dB.",
        "",
        "Saturation drives the",
        "output; it is on the",
        "front knob row too.",
        "",
        "Volume is -60 to",
        "+6 dB. The original",
        "went to -100, but the",
        "bottom 40 of those",
        "are all silence."
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "MIDI",
      "lines": [
        "Bend by Bend Range,",
        "0-12 st.",
        "",
        "Aftertouch bends by",
        "AT Range, -2 to +2 st",
        "- negative bends down.",
        "",
        "Mod wheel (CC 1)",
        "opens the sustain all",
        "the way up.",
        "",
        "CC 64 sustain holds",
        "notes. CC 68 is",
        "Legato. CC 120/123",
        "all notes off.",
        "",
        "Fine Tune detunes the",
        "whole instrument by",
        "+/-100 cents.",
        "",
        "Vel Sens sets how far",
        "velocity moves the",
        "sound; at 0 every",
        "note plays as 80."
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "Presets",
      "lines": [
        "Nine, from Punk Labs:",
        "",
        "J-Bass",
        "Defender",
        "Demonster",
        "Disco",
        "Flatworm",
        "Gargantuan",
        "Justice",
        "New Strings",
        "Sitcom",
        "",
        "They set the string,",
        "EQ, Mix and MIDI",
        "pages, and reset the",
        "switches added by",
        "this port: Glide,",
        "Glide Time, Frets,",
        "Ring, Alt Pick,",
        "Retrigger.",
        "",
        "Style, Mute and",
        "Legato are left",
        "alone - they are how",
        "you are playing, not",
        "what the patch is."
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "Credits",
      "lines": [
        "OneTrick CHONK",
        "(c) 2024 Punk Labs LLC",
        "punklabs.com/ot-chonk",
        "",
        "The synth is their",
        "Faust code, built for",
        "Move. The bass model",
        "is entirely theirs.",
        "",
        "It is free as in",
        "rights, not as in",
        "beer. If you play",
        "this, buy a copy.",
        "",
        "GPL-3.0-or-later.",
        "",
        "Move port by",
        "legsmechanical."
      ]
    }
  ]
}
